    13  ## Source, builds, and evidence
    14
    15  - Durable standalone Ahoi desktop changes belong in [the tracked overlay](overlay/chromium/README.md); upstream Chromium changes belong in [the patch stack](patches/chromium/README.md). `patches/chromium/series` owns patch order. Do not leave unique product changes only in `.work/chromium/src/`.
    16  - Read [BUILDING.md](docs/BUILDING.md) before source integration or builds. Use the guarded scripts, including `./scripts/build-ahoi.sh dev` for the documented development path; do not bypass overlay, pin, toolchain, or provenance checks.
    17  - Preserve Chromium's native profile, WebContents, sandbox, and permission ownership. Consult the relevant architecture document before changing those boundaries.
    18  - Bind visible E2E and subsequent focused tests to the exact integrated candidate. `./scripts/test-repository.sh` is a repository regression entry point, not installed-browser acceptance. Build, package, install, visible runtime, and release are separate evidence gates.

